WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
RUFUS: It's doing more for AI litigation
avoidance, certainly.

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:06.820
ALEX: Here's where the argument gets
sharp, and this is the exchange I

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.230
ALEX: want the room to actually have.
Jamie, you've been saying the real

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.639
ALEX: value is in agents like Muse
rather than heavy reasoning models like

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:17.049
ALEX: Astra. But Muse is doing task
execution. Astra is doing reasoning. Are

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:20.459
ALEX: those actually competing —

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:22.196
ALEX: or are they serving different
problems?

00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:24.413
JAMIE: For most people, the agent wins.

00:00:24.513 --> 00:00:27.885
RUFUS: Meta is betting that the person
who wants an AI to negotiate

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:31.257
RUFUS: a car sale is a larger market
than the person who wants

00:00:31.257 --> 00:00:34.629
RUFUS: an AI to solve a Tier 4 math
problem.
